@coderabbitai Valid; fixed in 0df1ebc5e1. I checked `eliminateDuplicates` in gh v2.105.0 (the installed version): it keeps only the newest run per name/workflow/event, so a pass followed by a same-key cancellation never reached the filter.

`release_checks` now reads the GraphQL `statusCheckRollup` of the PR head (paginated, not deduplicated). Each name/workflow/event key takes its newest non-cancelled verdict, so a same-key pass then cancel resolves to pass. A key with only cancellations is dropped only when a same-named key passed. Failures, unmatched cancellations, pending or queued runs, and empty or all-skipped suites still refuse. Callers that hold the head to be signed or merged now also bind the rollup to that exact head.

Verified with 10 synthetic rollups, including this case: ACCEPT, as expected. On the live package PRs, both accept at their head and refuse a wrong head. `process` dry-run still reports "would request release approval", and `test-cloudron-release-approval.sh` passes.

