@coderabbitai Confirmed and fixed in b1ef419490. `read` stopped at the first newline, so in a value that spans lines, every entry after the first newline was silently dropped.

`_target_files` now turns newlines into commas before splitting, then trims each entry as before. Both `$'README.md,\n.agents/AGENTS.md'` and one-path-per-line input (for example `git diff --name-only` output) now give the same stdout as the comma-separated list, with no warning. A space-separated value still warns.

I added both multi-line cases to `test-prework-discovery-helper.sh`. The README-only log differs from the combined log (131 vs 138 commits over 14 days), so the `cmp` assertions would catch the old truncation. The suite passes under Homebrew bash and `/bin/bash` 3.2.57, and ShellCheck is clean.

